  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The state of Iowa has recorded $1.7B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Obligations fell 53.1% year over year. Federal buyers issued 21,194 awards with an average award size of $80K. Year-to-date totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress. Obligations peaked at $3.6B in FY25 and then dropped to $1.7B in FY26. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $1.1B. Other large buying agencies include the Department of the Treasury with $204M and the Department of Agriculture with $128M. The largest vendors receiving obligations in Iowa include ROCKWELL COLLINS, INC. at $394M and DATA LINK SOLUTIONS LLC at $294M. Industries with the biggest obligations in FY2026 to date include Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $360M and Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying at $137M. These figures represent contract obligations through the current fiscal year to date and reflect where federal buying activity is concentrated in Iowa right now.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies drive federal buying in Iowa?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $1.1B. The Department of the Treasury obligated $204M and the Department of Agriculture obligated $128M. Multiple civilian agencies including the Department of Veterans Affairs and the Department of Energy also contributed, obligating $68.4M and $44.3M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who captures the largest federal obligations in Iowa?",
        "body": "ROCKWELL COLLINS, INC. captured $394M in obligations and DATA LINK SOLUTIONS LLC captured $294M. PMX INDUSTRIES, INC. captured $137M while AMERICAN ORDNANCE LLC captured $92.1M. Iowa State University of Science and Technology received $45M and several construction and services firms appear on the list as well."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Iowa?",
      "a": "Answer: $1.7B in federal contract obligations went to Iowa for FY2026 to date. The state received 21,194 awards with an average award size of $80K. These totals are fiscal year to date and current-year totals are partial."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Iowa?",
      "a": "Answer: The Department of Defense, the Department of the Treasury, and the Department of Agriculture award the most contracts in Iowa. The Department of Defense obligated $1.1B, the Department of the Treasury obligated $204M, and the Department of Agriculture obligated $128M in FY2026 to date."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest federal contractors in Iowa?",
      "a": "Answer: ROCKWELL COLLINS, INC. and DATA LINK SOLUTIONS LLC are the largest federal contractors in Iowa by obligations. ROCKWELL COLLINS, INC. received $394M and DATA LINK SOLUTIONS LLC received $294M in FY2026 to date."
